            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="FAL01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Henry Thomas</forename>
                        <surname>Carey</surname>
                        <addName>eighth Viscount Falkland</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1766-02-27">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1796-05-28"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> See Taylor, <title>Records of My Life</title> where Henry Thomas Carey (eighth Viscount Falkland) is linked with <persName key="KIN01">John 'Jew' King</persName>, 
    with whom most of the contacts take place.  The entries are to Falkland, but there are a number of entries in 1795 to Carey, who is identified as Falkland's successor to the title,
    <persName key="FAL02">Charles John Carey</persName>.  There are two entries to Falkland after Henry Thomas Carey's death in 1796, which have been identified as references to his successor.
  </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">John Taylor, <title>Records of my Life</title>, 2 vols (London, 1832)</bibl>
